    "test_pr": 169,
    "problem_statement": "The NimBLE host advertising-data interface is being reworked. The ble_hs_adv_fields structure must hold its UUID fields as typed BLE UUID objects rather than raw integers/bytes: uuids16 must be an array of ble_uuid16_t, uuids32 an array of ble_uuid32_t, and uuids128 an array of ble_uuid128_t (instead of uint16_t*/uint32_t*/void*). When advertising fields are encoded to raw HCI advertising data, each 16/32/128-bit UUID must be written using its ble_uuid value (16-bit UUIDs via ble_uuid_flat, 32-bit UUIDs as the actual 32-bit little-endian value, 128-bit UUIDs via ble_uuid_flat). The invalid/OOB-only advertising data types (Class of Device, LE Bluetooth Device Address, LE Role, and the non-usable BLE_HS_ADV_TYPE_* defines) must be removed from the struct and from encoding/parsing. Host-to-application discovery reports (ble_gap_disc_desc) must carry only the raw advertising buffer (data/length_data) instead of a parsed ble_hs_adv_fields pointer; callers parse the raw buffer themselves via ble_hs_adv_parse_fields, and limited-discovery filtering is done by locating the flags field via a raw field search. The unit tests in net/nimble/host/test must be able to populate and verify these typed UUID fields in ble_hs_adv_fields.",
    "platform": "native",
    "test_path": "net/nimble/host/test",
